<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Jan producer price index up 9.2 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>S.African Jan producer price index up 9.2 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's all-commodities producer price index rose 0.8 percent in January from December after rising 1.0 percent in December, Central Statistical Service figures show.</p>
<p>The year-on-year rise in January was 9.2 percent after December's 8.8 percent rise.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast PPI would rise 1.0 percent month-on-month and 9.4 percent year-on-year.  </p>
<p>    Pct changes:	     Year/year		    month/month</p>
<p>			 Jan '97   Dec '96   Jan '96  - latest   prev</p>
<p>All commodities    9.2	 8.8	 7.2	  0.8	1.0</p>
<p>Locally produced   9.2	 8.5	 7.8	  0.9	0.7</p>
<p>Imported	     9.6	 9.3	 4.7	  0.6	1.8</p>
<p>Index (base 1995=100):</p>
<p>			 Jan '97   Dec '96   Jan '96</p>
<p>All commodities    112.3     111.4     102.8</p>
<p>Locally produced   112.9     111.9     103.4</p>
<p>Imported	     110.7     110.0     101.0</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
